          </span>
          <span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <span class="block h-1.5 w-10 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
            <span class="block h-1.5 w-12 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .35"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 3. CONTEST ENTRY & ELIGIBILITY — moved directly under Web3. The %>
  <%# walked entry flow (glow follows), plus the honest web2/web3 map. %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section id="modals-contest-entry" class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Contest entry &amp; eligibility</h3>
        <% if age_gate_on %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-success); border-color: var(--color-success)">age gate on</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-warning); border-color: var(--color-warning)">age gate off</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The pre-entry gate and the full entry flow. The age bar is enforced HERE,
        but its two cards &mdash;
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/blocks/_birthday</code> (the
        ask) and <code class="font-mono text-2xs">_age_gate</code> (the refusal)
        &mdash; are shown in the <strong>Profile</strong> section, because they are
        about who the account is. Both are engine primitives gated by
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">Studio.feature?(:age_gate)</code>, and their
        minimum age, jurisdiction label, endpoint, and legal copy are all
        <strong>app-supplied</strong> (the engine hardcodes no policy). The entry flow is
        a <strong>walked sequence</strong> &mdash; <strong>Entry tokens &rarr; Payment
        processing &rarr; Entry Tokens Minted &rarr; Contest enter processing &rarr;
        Contest entered</strong> &mdash; and the live card <strong>glows</strong>,
        following the step machine (the two load steps honor the same min-duration
        convention as Web3 above).
      </p>
      <%# The web2/web3 finding — a real divergence, stated honestly, not invented. %>
      <div class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-subtle bg-surface p-3 text-xs text-secondary leading-snug">
        <p class="text-heading font-semibold mb-1">Web2 vs web3 — the honest map</p>
        <p class="mb-1">
          The two funding paths <strong>diverge at the front-end and the entry-submit
          endpoint, then converge</strong>. <strong>Web2</strong> (card / Stripe /
          Coinflow / PayPal) mints one prepaid entry token per credit on-chain after
          payment clears, then <strong>consumes</strong> one token to enter.
          <strong>Web3</strong> (wallet / USDC on-chain) funds USDC directly and
          <strong>mints no token</strong> &mdash; the mint&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;consume prelude
          is web2-only.
        </p>
        <p>
          Both create the <strong>same on-chain Entry PDA</strong> and resolve to the
          <strong>same “Entry Confirmed” card</strong>. The walk below demos the web2
          path end-to-end; web3 skips the mint and joins at
          <strong>enter&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;entered</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <%# The birthday / age-gate CARDS live in the Profile section — they are
          about who the account is, and grouping them by subject beats grouping
          them by the moment they happen to be asked. ENFORCEMENT still lives
          here: the bar is checked at contest entry, which is what this section is
          named for. The demo walk is unbroken — confirming the birthday card
          still advances to Entry tokens below, via the page-level 'age-verified'
          wiring, which the rename did NOT touch precisely because consuming apps
          already listen on it. %>

      <%# 1. Entry tokens — the picker (walk's entry). Picking a pack advances. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Entry tokens",
            reference: %(the "Entry tokens" picker (app-specific — documented composing studio/modals/blocks chrome). The packs, pricing, rails, and on-chain mint stay app-owned. Picking a pack walks Payment processing -> Minted -> enter -> entered. Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'picker' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'picker' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "picker", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 space-y-2">
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-primary)"></span>
          <span class="block h-6 w-full rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 2. Payment processing — the mint-at-purchase load step (web2). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Payment processing",
            reference: %(the "Payment processing" step (entry-tokens step 'confirming') — "Confirming your purchase…" over "Payment cleared — a server job mints one prepaid entry credit per token on-chain." A load modal; honors the min-duration convention then auto-advances to Entry Tokens Minted. Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'confirming', mintedCount: 3, mintedBalance: '3' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'confirming', mintedCount: 3, mintedBalance: '3' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "confirming", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="loading-dots mx-auto"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 3. Entry Tokens Minted — ready to consume at entry (hold to confirm). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Entry Tokens Minted",
            reference: %(the "Entry Tokens Minted" step (entry-tokens step 'minted') — "You now have N available." Holding to confirm consumes one token on-chain to create the contest entry (advances to Contest enter processing). Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'minted', mintedCount: 3, mintedBalance: '3' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'minted', mintedCount: 3, mintedBalance: '3' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "minted", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 15%, transparent)">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold" style="color: var(--color-primary)">3</span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 4. Contest enter processing — the on-chain consume load step. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Contest enter processing",
            reference: %(the "Contest enter processing" step (entry-tokens step 'entering') — "Confirming your entry…" over "Consuming one token on-chain to create your contest entry." A load modal; honors the min-duration convention then auto-advances to Contest entered. Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'entering' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'entering' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "entering", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="loading-dots mx-auto"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# 5. Contest entered — the shared Entry Confirmed finish (web2 + web3 converge). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Contest entered",
            reference: %(the "Contest entered" success (entry-tokens step 'entered') — "Good Luck / Entry Confirmed" with the branded on-chain tx link and a Contest Lobby CTA. The SAME finish both web2 and web3 entries converge on. Open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'entered', txSignature: '…' })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-tokens', { step: 'entered', txSignature: '5xTrDemoEntrySignature1234567890abc' })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("entry-tokens", step: "entered", step_default: "picker") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-success) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-success)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# it-begins — the moment a contest locks. The DRAINING CTA is the whole
          card: it interrupts someone mid-page at a moment they did not choose,
          and the drain is what gives them a say in what happens next. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "It Begins",
            reference: %(the contest-lock announcement (style/modals/_it_begins) — turf-monster's modals/_it_begins, fired when a contest's lock countdown reaches zero. APP-SPECIFIC: the engine owns no contests and no lock. It lends blocks/_cta_redirect — the DRAINING button, which is the whole reason this card is worth a specimen and the one part you have to WATCH rather than read, because a timer is not visible in markup. This card interrupts someone mid-page at a moment they did not choose: a dismissible modal would leave them on a stale board, a hard redirect would yank the page away, and the drain is the middle — it announces what is about to happen and gives them the length of the bar to opt out. Shortened to 4 seconds here (production runs 8) so the drain can be watched twice; it redirects NOWHERE — the block's null-destination gallery mode, so the drain completes and the card stays openable instead of ending as a stuck spinner. Open with $store.dsModals.open('it-begins')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('it-begins')",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("it-begins") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">🏟️</div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-28 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
          <%# the CTA mid-drain — the bar empties, and leaving is the way out %>
          <span class="block h-5 w-full rounded overflow-hidden" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-cta) 25%, transparent)">
            <span class="block h-full rounded" style="width: 55%; background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
          </span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 5. SYSTEM AND STATUS (reusable card blocks) %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section id="modals-system-status" class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">System &amp; status</h3>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The reusable card blocks under <code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/blocks/</code> &mdash;
        the studio-canonical processing, success, error, and countdown states.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Processing",
            reference: %(the "Processing" card block (studio/modals/blocks/_processing_card) — open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-processing')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-processing')" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 animate-spin" style="border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-cta) 30%, transparent); border-top-color: var(--color-cta)"></div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Success",
            reference: %(the "Success" card block (studio/modals/blocks/_success_card, entry-confirmed style) — open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-success')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-success')" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-success) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-success)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Error / retry",
            reference: %(the "Error" card block (studio/modals/blocks/_error_card) — open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-error')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-error')" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">⚠️</div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-20 mx-auto rounded border" style="border-color: var(--color-border-strong)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Countdown",
            reference: %(the "Countdown" progress block (studio/modals/blocks/_progress_countdown) — open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-countdown')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-countdown')" } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <div class="w-full rounded-full overflow-hidden" style="height: 6px; background: rgba(128,128,128,0.2)">
            <div style="height: 100%; width: 60%; border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--color-cta)"></div>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-16 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# rate-limit-general — the SOFT cap. Dismissible, apologetic, and it
          auto-closes when the wait elapses rather than making anyone
          acknowledge a penalty for clicking too fast. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Rate limited (soft)",
            reference: %(the soft rate-limit wait (style/modals/_rate_limit_general) — turf-monster's modals/_rate_limit_general, opened by the authedFetch 429 interceptor when a general-tier cap trips. Composes the engine's blocks/_card_header; the engine throttles nothing. THE TONE IS THE DESIGN: this is a soft cap on someone who did nothing wrong, so the card is dismissible, the copy is "Easy there" rather than an error, and it AUTO-CLOSES when the wait elapses instead of demanding an acknowledgement. The countdown is seeded from the 429's own Retry-After, so the number is the server's rather than a guess. It also clears its interval in a destroy() METHOD — Alpine 3 dispatches no "destroy" DOM event, so an @destroy listener never fires and the timer outlives every close. Shortened to 10 seconds here so the auto-close can be watched. Open with $store.dsModals.open('rate-limit-general', { secondsLeft: 10 })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('rate-limit-general', { secondsLeft: 10 })",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("rate-limit-general") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">✋</div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-28 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
          <%# a dismiss link, not a button — the soft cap has no penalty to accept %>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-12 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .3"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# rail-row — the funding picker's option row. Exactly ONE primary. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Rail row",
            reference: %(the funding rail row (studio/modals/blocks/_rail_row) — the option row a funding hub is built from, ported out of turf-monster where the SAME markup appeared TEN times across modals/_onramp_hub, _buy_entry_token and _wallet_topup. The specimen shows three: one :primary and two :neutral, which is the arrangement a real hub uses. The emphasis is a RANKING, not decoration — a hub of equally-weighted rails asks the person to compare payment processors, which is not a question they can answer. It reads louder in three places at once (doubled border, filled hover, coloured chevron) because one alone is invisible on a 56px row, which is why it is ONE `emphasis:` local rather than three classes a callsite could half-apply. Brand colour rides in as `icon_bg`, so a rail wears a processor's mark with no asset shipped; the emoji tile passes icon_class: "text-xl", because the default bold-white treatment renders an emoji as a fuzzy white blob. Open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-rail-row')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-rail-row')",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("ds-rail-row") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 space-y-2">
          <%# the primary rail, then two neutrals — the ranking IS the thumbnail %>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md p-1.5" style="border: 2px solid var(--color-primary)">
            <span class="block h-4 w-4 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
            <span class="block h-1.5 flex-1 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .3"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md p-1.5 border border-subtle">
            <span class="block h-4 w-4 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .25"></span>
            <span class="block h-1.5 flex-1 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md p-1.5 border border-subtle">
            <span class="block h-4 w-4 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .25"></span>
            <span class="block h-1.5 flex-1 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          </span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# close-x — the mark, and the one class it depends on. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Close ×",
            reference: %(the centred-title card's close mark (studio/modals/blocks/_close_x) — ported out of turf-monster where this markup appeared BYTE-IDENTICAL in eight files (modals/_wallet_deposit, _wallet_topup, _cdp_ramp, _onramp_hub, _buy_entry_token, and three under modals/auth/). It exists ALONGSIDE blocks/_shell rather than inside it: the shell puts its title on the left with the close beside it, while this family centres the title and positions the mark above it, so retrofitting the shell would move eight titles — a visual change wearing a refactor's clothes. THE PARENT MUST BE `relative`: the button is absolute, so it anchors to the nearest positioned ancestor, and without that class it climbs to the modal host's backdrop and lands in the page corner. Nothing errors and nothing in the markup reads as wrong, which is why the specimen says so out loud. Open with $store.dsModals.open('ds-close-x')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('ds-close-x')",
            glow_when: ds_glow.call("ds-close-x") } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2 relative">
          <span class="absolute top-1 right-2 text-secondary leading-none">&times;</span>
          <span class="block h-2 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-28 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 6. TEMPLATES (copy-from archetypes) %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section id="modals-templates" class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Templates</h3>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        Reusable archetypes under <code class="font-mono text-2xs">studio/modals/templates/</code> &mdash;
        the copy-from reference cards for a new modal (wizard, form, action,
        status, success).
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
      <% [
           ["template-wizard",  "Wizard",  "🧭", "studio/modals/templates/_wizard"],
           ["template-form",    "Form",    "📝", "studio/modals/templates/_form"],
           ["template-action",  "Action",  "❓", "studio/modals/templates/_action"],
           ["template-status",  "Status",  "⏳", "studio/modals/templates/_status"],
           ["template-success", "Success", "✅", "studio/modals/templates/_success"]
         ].each do |id, label, glyph, partial| %>
        <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
              label:     label,
              reference: %(the "#{label}" modal template (#{partial}) — open with $store.dsModals.open('#{id}')),
              open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('#{id}')" } do %>
          <div class="pointer-events-none w-32 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
            <div class="text-2xl leading-none"><%= glyph %></div>
            <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
            <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity: .6"></span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <%# 7. REWARDS / leveling (gated by Studio.feature?(:leveling)) %>
  <%# ===================================================================== %>
  <section id="modals-rewards" class="space-y-5">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-heading">Rewards</h3>
        <% if leveling_on %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-success); border-color: var(--color-success)">enabled on this app</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="badge" style="color: var(--color-warning); border-color: var(--color-warning)">disabled on this app</span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm">
        The seeds bar + level-up celebrations, gated by
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">Studio.feature?(:leveling)</code> — an
        app-level setting <strong>independent of :web3</strong> (some apps have
        Solana but no leveling). Leveling is <strong><%= leveling_on ? "on" : "off" %></strong>
        here, so these render
        <%= leveling_on ? "live." : "greyed and badged — but STILL openable as a preview." %>
        The seed counts, level, and free entry are <strong>app-supplied props</strong>
        (<code class="font-mono text-2xs">seedsEarned</code>,
        <code class="font-mono text-2xs">seedsTotal</code>, …) — the engine renders
        the bar, the app feeds the numbers.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Level up",
            reference: %(the Rewards "Level up" celebration (studio/modals/blocks/_success_card with the sheen + studio-glow badge) — open with $store.dsModals.open('levelup')),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('levelup')",
            disabled: !leveling_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">🎉</div>
          <span class="inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-white text-sm font-extrabold" style="background: var(--color-cta)">10</span>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Entry + seeds — the SAME _entry_confirmed card, now with seedsEarned
          crossing a level so the :leveling seeds bar mounts in the _success_card
          yield and plays the 4-phase level-up (fill → pop → drain → refill), then
          swaps to the Free Entry Earned reward line. %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Entry + seeds level-up",
            reference: %(the Rewards "Entry + seeds" celebration (studio/modals/blocks/_entry_confirmed — the :leveling seeds bar + Free Entry Earned reward injected into _success_card's yield) — open with $store.dsModals.open('entry-confirmed', { txSignature: '…', lobbyUrl: null, seedsEarned: 30, seedsTotal: 100 })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('entry-confirmed', { txSignature: '5xTrDemoSignature1234567890abcXYZ', lobbyUrl: null, seedsEarned: 30, seedsTotal: 100 })",
            disabled: !leveling_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="mx-auto w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 15%, transparent)">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" style="color: var(--color-primary)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-1">
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity:.6"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta); opacity:.25"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity:.12"></span>
            <span class="flex-1 h-2.5 rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity:.12"></span>
          </div>
          <span class="block h-4 w-full rounded" style="background: var(--color-cta)"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Free Entry Earned — the standalone level-up reward modal (:leveling). %>
      <%= render layout: "style/modal_specimen", locals: {
            label:     "Free Entry Earned",
            reference: %(the Rewards "Free Entry Earned" level-up modal (studio/modals/blocks/_free_entry_earned) — open with $store.dsModals.open('free-entry-earned', { level: 3 })),
            open_expr: "$store.dsModals.open('free-entry-earned', { level: 3 })",
            disabled: !leveling_on, openable: true } do %>
        <div class="pointer-events-none w-40 rounded-lg bg-surface border border-subtle shadow p-4 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="text-2xl leading-none">🎉</div>
          <span class="block h-2 w-20 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .18"></span>
          <span class="block h-1.5 w-24 mx-auto rounded" style="background: var(--color-text); opacity: .12"></span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

</section>
